HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5ecf85f5, "a `str` is built by this runtime, so no C header holds one: declare it `cstr` and read it with `validated`, which copies and may fail (\302\2474.20)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_612fabdb, "a `constant` names a value, and `()` is a type rather than a value");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_76e6282d, "a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted, and this asks the header for one of C's. Declare it `ptr` if the program only hands it back to C");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_760ac0ad, "a `str` is this runtime's own value, with a reference count before its bytes, so no C struct holds one: declare the field `cstr` and read it with `validated`, which copies and may fail");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_380698fc, "a C struct holds a pointer to its elements, never the elements: declare the field `ptr` and reach them through the header's own accessors");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7357b0c8, "`T?` is this language's own two-word value and no header declares one: a C function reports failure in its result or an out-parameter (\302\2474.19)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_32c7b346, "`()` is a type rather than a value, so nothing can hold one \342\200\224 drop the field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_59aa1d79, "a record can hold another only if the header declares that one too: move it into this `extern` group, or declare the field `ptr` if C holds a pointer to it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c535382, "this group has no spelling for that: a field is a number, `bool`, `ptr`, `cstr`, another record of the group, or a fixed array of one");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3855f106, "`()` names no value, so there is no argument to pass: as a *result* it is C's `void`, which a parameter list has no spelling for. Drop the parameter, or declare the type the header uses");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_26f94c26, "an `@` parameter is C's out-parameter, so this asks C to WRITE a function value here, and a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted. Declare it `@");
